    <string name="push_wakeups">Wake-ups through UnifiedPush</string>
    <string name="push_status_off">Off. Needs a distributor app such as ntfy.</string>
    <string name="push_status_unsupported">Your server doesn\'t offer wake-ups yet</string>
    <string name="push_status_no_distributor">No distributor app found. Install one such as ntfy, then turn this on again.</string>
    <string name="push_status_registering">Setting up with your distributor app…</string>
    <string name="push_status_failed">Your distributor app couldn\'t set this up (%1$s). Open it, then turn this off and on.</string>
    <string name="push_status_refused">Your server only accepts wake-ups through %1$s. In ntfy, set the default server to https://%1$s, then turn this off and on.</string>
    <string name="push_status_refused_other">Your server didn\'t accept the wake-up address from your distributor app.</string>
    <string name="push_status_pending">Waiting to reach your server</string>
    <string name="push_status_active">On, through %1$s</string>
    <string name="push_explainer">A distributor app such as ntfy can wake Meldiq when something arrives, so Meldiq doesn\'t have to keep its own connection open. A wake-up carries nothing from your messages: Meldiq then fetches them, still encrypted, straight from your server. First set ntfy\'s default server to %1$s. Keep \"Stay connected in background\" on until wake-ups show as on.</string>
    <string name="push_host_unknown">the push server your community gives you</string>
    <string name="push_fetching">Checking for new messages</string>
    <string name="call_e2ee">End-to-end encrypt call media</string>
    <string name="call_e2ee_on">On: calls won\'t join without the key. The call screen says \"End-to-end encrypted\" only once media has actually decrypted.</string>
    <string name="call_e2ee_off">Off: media is protected in transit only</string>
    <string name="call_hw_aec">Use the phone\'s echo canceller</string>
    <string name="call_hw_aec_on">On: this phone\'s built-in echo cancellation. Turn off if people you call hear their own voice.</string>
    <string name="call_hw_aec_off">Off (recommended): Meldiq\'s own echo cancellation, the same on every phone. Applies from the next call.</string>
